1	/**
2	 * SFCC-11 plan step 4.6 — cartDrawerContainer.tsx's own wiring contract. This step's own text
3	 * calls this the highest-risk piece in the plan ("a mistake here is exactly as invisible to any
4	 * single piece's own per-file review" as the earlier step 3.5 insertion was) — every dependency
5	 * this file wires together already has its own exhaustive test suite (ZimmCartDrawer,
6	 * cartItemMapper, useCartMergeAndCap, useCartMessages, ZimmCartItemActions, ZimmCartEmptyState,
7	 * ZimmCartButtonGroup, useWishlistAuthDrawer). Per testing.md's own scoping guidance, this file
8	 * mocks every one of those at its own smallest surface and asserts ONLY this container's own
9	 * contract: does it call each dependency with the right values, at the right time, and does it
10	 * make the right empty-vs-populated / guest-vs-registered decisions — not whether those
11	 * dependencies themselves behave correctly in isolation, which is already proven elsewhere.
12	 *
13	 * ZimmCartDrawer itself is the one dependency NOT mocked — it is small, already fully covered by
14	 * its own suite, and rendering it for real here is what actually proves pass criterion 5's second
15	 * half ("this container is what decides between the real item list and ZimmCartEmptyState"),
16	 * rather than merely a mocked component recording which children prop it was given.
17	 */
